{
  "id": "starter-triple-get-campaign",
  "name": "Starter Triple Get Campaign",
  "category": "campaign",
  "description": {
    "text": "The Starter Triple Get Campaign ran in Japan from 1 December 2001 to 30 April 2002, tied to the e-Card starter deck. Each deck held a postcard: players stuck on the proofs of purchase of three starter decks, picked one of two courses and mailed it in. The Red/Green course was Venusaur, Blastoise and Charizard, and the Gold/Silver course Meganium, Feraligatr and Typhlosion, holofoil versions of the last evolutions of the Kanto and Johto starter Pokémon that the main set printed without holofoil; each winner got all three of their course, in a Pokémon card game envelope with a winning notice. After each of five monthly deadlines 1,000 winners were drawn for each course, 5,000 per course in all by Pokumon's count, so 5,000 copies of each card were given out.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Pokumon: Starter Triple Get Campaign",
        "url": "https://pokumon.com/starter-triple-get-campaign/"
      },
      {
        "title": "Pokumon: Charizard (014/P Japanese Promo)",
